--TEST--
A body that is not one whole JSON document is a `ParseError` from `Core\Request::json()`, and a body the peer never sent is the same refusal rather than `null` `rule:errors/ambiguous-input-refused`
--HEADERS--
Content-Type: application/json
--POST_RAW--
{"name": "ada"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The peer declared `application/json` and sent something else: the class is
// `ParseError`, which spec § 10 puts under `RuntimeError` as "input did not
// match a format this code declared", and it is what a handler maps to 400.
// It is never a `LogicError`, because a peer must not be able to make a
// program report its own defect.
try {
    Core\Request::json();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $malformed) {
    echo "malformed rejected\n";
}

// The refusal is the reading, not a claim on the body: the reader that copies
// the octets out still answers them, so a handler can log what arrived. The
// `--POST_RAW--` section's own closing newline is part of the body the peer
// sent, so this line writes no second one.
echo Core\Request::body();

// And every later call refuses the same way, off the same held octets.
try {
    Core\Request::json();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $again) {
    echo "still rejected\n";
}
--EXPECT--
malformed rejected
{"name": "ada"
still rejected
